,"_gate_insider_own":0.07535,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":50.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Kforce Inc. provides professional staffing services and solutions in the United States. It operates through two segments, Technology, and Finance and Accounting (FA). The Technology segment provides talent solutions to its clients in disciplines, such as systems and applications architecture and development; data management and analytics; cloud architecture and engineering; business and artificial intelligence; machine learning; project and program management; and network architecture and security. This segment serves clients in the financial and business services, communications, insurance, retail, and technology industries. Its FA segment offers talent solutions to its clients in finance and accounting roles, including financial planning and analysis, business intelligence analysis, general accounting, transactional accounting, business and cost analysis, and taxation and treasury, as well as consultants in mortgage servicing, customer and call center support, data entry, and other administrative roles. This segment serves clients in various industries, including financial and business services, healthcare, and manufacturing sectors. The company was founded in 1962 and is headquartered in Tampa, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph J. Liberatore | CEO, President & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $831K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Kforce, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.0B market cap on $1.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and +0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 37% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 28-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The business throws off $47M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.77\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 7.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 7.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.13904186485462233},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(KFRC) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/15/KFRC_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_110926062401_1794223441.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794223441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Kforce (NASDAQ:KFRC) Stock: Insider David Dunkel Sells 500 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/kforce-nasdaqkfrc-stock-insider-david-dunkel-sells-500-shares.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794055748.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Insider Transaction: David L Dunkel Sells $174K Worth Of Kforce Shares","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/62982301/insider-transaction-david-l-dunkel-sells-174k-worth-kforce-shares","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793977316.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Have Kforce Insiders Been Selling Stock?","source":"simplywall.st